  title={VI. CONCLUSION This paper explored two methods of data representation: sequences of events and sequence matrices, along with the SLRI window approach to train the GRU model with and without the embedding layer. The work evaluated these methods using both SLRI and SLCD windows to simulate the clinical setting, on an administrative dataset of over 240,000 individuals with AMH to develop a predictive tool for multiple outcomes. We found that using sequence matrix representation outperformed sequence of events representation for both SLRI and SLCD windows by over 20\% in both AUC and sensitivity in this cohort.},
